### Health check
GET http://localhost:8080/

###

### 1. Register a new user
# @name register
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "testuser",
  "email": "test@scent.dev",
  "password": "password123",
  "displayName": "Test User"
}

###

### 2. Login with the registered user
# @name login
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test@scent.dev",
  "password": "password123"
}

###

### 3. Get current user — uses token captured from login response above
# In IntelliJ HTTP Client, run login first, then this will auto-populate.
# For curl: replace {{login.response.body.$.token}} with the actual token.
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}
